# Byte-exact working tree. This file must be the FIRST commit, before any
# clone exists.
#
# `scripts/run_acceptance.py:source_digest()` hashes the RAW BYTES of every
# shipped file — over 200 paths, including `LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt`, which is
# separately pinned by sha256 in tests/unit/test_release_integrity.py.
# Git's default `text=auto` rewrites line endings on checkout on Windows and
# on any host with core.autocrlf set. A rewritten tree produces a different
# `tree_digest` and a different AGPL hash, and the failure surfaces as
# ACC-TREE-1 "a different tree" and R-LICENSE "wrong licence text" — neither
# of which says "line endings", so the cause is not discoverable from the
# symptom.
#
# `* -text` disables all end-of-line conversion for every path. Nothing in
# this repository wants normalisation: the digest is the point.
* -text

# Binary, marked so git never attempts a diff or a merge on them.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary
*.wasm  binary
